    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d900">

                <pb facs="0816" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/15190.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-10T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 10, 1915—11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>623. Instead of only promising prospects of unification it was decided in the
                    Convention yesterday that the new executive put in force the law establishing a
                    committee of public health for the undefined purpose of punishing the enemies of
                    the revolution besides the confiscation of their houses and effects which is
                    already being done on great scale. All this will certainly add a régime of
                    terror to that of famine. On the other hand I am confidentially informed from
                    Vera Cruz that the forces of General Carranza are approaching Mexico expecting
                    to occupy it next week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
